From 30494489c8bc8d83631b6ca96c9128e37c8b89c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WINQ-EMU Dev <dev@winq-emu.local>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 15:54:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus+vrend: Windows dma-buf shim checkpoint (Zink + VA-API
 working)

Stable baseline after rolling back the VAAPI shadow-memory and
video-plane pre-registration experiments that broke Vulkan allocations
and caused Zink/VA-API regressions.

Kept in this checkpoint:
- Windows dma-buf shim: synthesize VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf and
  VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier on top of the Intel Windows Vulkan
  ICD, with DMA_BUF <-> OPAQUE_WIN32 NT-HANDLE translation in both
  vkAllocateMemory import and vkr_device_memory_export_blob paths.
  Guest opt-out via WINQ_DMABUF_SHIM_OFF=1.
- R/B channel fix: the EGL dma-buf R<->B swap in
  vrend_create_sampler_view is now gated on !VREND_STORAGE_GL_MEMOBJ so
  the Windows GL_EXT_memory_object_win32 import path is not double-
  swapped (fixes vkcube xcb, SuperTuxKart, Haruna+Zink).
- GL_EXT_memory_object_win32 import: vrend can attach Vulkan-exported
  NT HANDLEs to GL textures for the Zink-on-Wayland compositor.

Verified manually (user): vulkaninfo, Zink, mpv --hwdec=vaapi-copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
